WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:03.236
-My first guest is an
Emmy and Golden Globe winner

00:00:03.236 --> 00:00:04.904
and one of the
funniest people on the planet.

00:00:04.904 --> 00:00:06.573
The first two seasons of
his acclaimed series,

00:00:06.573 --> 00:00:08.674
"After Life," --
Gosh, it's a good show.

00:00:08.674 --> 00:00:11.744
It's such a good mix of
comedy and drama.

00:00:11.744 --> 00:00:12.878
He's awesome.

00:00:12.878 --> 00:00:14.714
They're available right now
on Netflix.

00:00:14.714 --> 00:00:16.816
Here's the one-and-only
Ricky Gervais!

00:00:16.816 --> 00:00:19.252
Hey! There he is.
That's what I'm talking about.

00:00:19.252 --> 00:00:22.422
Ricky Gervais, look at you, man.
You look fantastic.

00:00:22.422 --> 00:00:24.924
Wow! Thank you so much
for doing this.

00:00:24.924 --> 00:00:26.525
I appreciate this.

00:00:26.525 --> 00:00:29.696
I know you're in --
You're over in U.K. right now,

00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:31.630
so thank you for doing this.

00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:35.768
Last time we talked
was in April.

00:00:35.768 --> 00:00:37.169
We were on Zoom right --

00:00:37.169 --> 00:00:38.605
maybe like a month
into quarantine.

00:00:38.605 --> 00:00:41.340
And so thanks
for doing that, by the way.

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:43.409
-I haven't moved.

00:00:43.409 --> 00:00:45.545
I've been in this --
And nothing's happened.

00:00:45.545 --> 00:00:47.179
"Groundhog Day."

00:00:47.179 --> 00:00:48.648
I've been here.

00:00:48.648 --> 00:00:53.486
In fact, you might have well
rerun the interview from April.

00:00:53.486 --> 00:00:54.787
Nothing's happened.
-Nothing has changed?

00:00:54.787 --> 00:00:57.590
Nothing happened?
-Nothing changed.

00:00:57.590 --> 00:01:00.860
I'm probably wearing
the same T-shirt.

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:01.894
-Could we do that?

00:01:01.894 --> 00:01:03.329
We'll just run
the other interview.

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:04.330
Yeah, we might as well
just do it.

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:06.399
-No one would know.

00:01:06.399 --> 00:01:08.534
-Well, look,
the good news is that

00:01:08.534 --> 00:01:11.304
the vaccines
are being rolled out.

00:01:11.304 --> 00:01:12.672
-Yeah.

00:01:12.672 --> 00:01:15.742
-And they're -- I mean,
you're on the list, obviously.

00:01:15.742 --> 00:01:19.012
-I'm on the list,
but we checked, right?

00:01:19.012 --> 00:01:21.414
I wasn't even registered
to a doctor.

00:01:21.414 --> 00:01:22.881
I had to go online
to register --

00:01:22.881 --> 00:01:24.883
I don't go to the doctor.

00:01:24.883 --> 00:01:27.153
And I got registered.

00:01:27.153 --> 00:01:30.523
And you put in your details,
and it tells you where you are.

00:01:30.523 --> 00:01:32.892
And there's like 30 million
people ahead of me.

00:01:32.892 --> 00:01:35.728
How can I not be vulnerable?
Look at me.

00:01:35.728 --> 00:01:39.565
How can there people --
I mean, it's so annoying.

00:01:39.565 --> 00:01:41.200
I can't wait to get --

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:44.303
I will fight an old lady
for that vaccine.

00:01:44.303 --> 00:01:46.505
It will be like
"Game of Thrones."

00:01:46.505 --> 00:01:49.843
I will grab that.
-No.

00:01:49.843 --> 00:01:51.577
-I'll be like a deranged junkie.

00:01:51.577 --> 00:01:54.146
I will grab the needle
out of her arm.

00:01:54.146 --> 00:01:57.249
Of course I will.
-That's not true at all.

00:01:57.249 --> 00:02:00.086
-Do you know what, though?
Ah! See?

00:02:00.086 --> 00:02:04.790
My plan is -- alright? --
within the next few months,

00:02:04.790 --> 00:02:10.396
I'm going to be clinically obese
so I'll be high risk.

00:02:10.396 --> 00:02:12.398
I'll walk in and I'll go --

00:02:12.398 --> 00:02:14.167
I'll sit down.
I'll go, "Hello, Doctor."

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:17.369
[ Wheezes ]
And I'll be breathing heavily.

00:02:17.369 --> 00:02:18.704
And they'll go,

00:02:18.704 --> 00:02:21.874
"Jesus, let's get this fat
[bleep] injected.

00:02:21.874 --> 00:02:23.476
He's going to die," right?

00:02:23.476 --> 00:02:27.914
And then --
-This is a bad plan.

00:02:27.914 --> 00:02:32.251
No. This is a very bad plan.

00:02:32.251 --> 00:02:33.987
Do not do that. Oh, just don't.

00:02:33.987 --> 00:02:36.021
But, eventually,
we'll all get it,

00:02:36.021 --> 00:02:38.557
and then we'll talk
and we'll be happy to have you.

00:02:38.557 --> 00:02:40.159
Oh, you know what
I want to ask you about?

00:02:40.159 --> 00:02:41.894
I heard that there's
a new addition to the family,

00:02:41.894 --> 00:02:44.530
because I know
you're a huge animal lover.

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:46.799
And, like a lot of people
who are in quarantine,

00:02:46.799 --> 00:02:48.801
you started fostering
a cat, right?

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:49.835
-Well, yeah.

00:02:49.835 --> 00:02:53.839
Our lovely cat, Ollie,
of 16 years

00:02:53.839 --> 00:02:56.041
died at the beginning
of lockdown.

00:02:56.041 --> 00:02:58.644
And I thought, "We're not going
to get one now," right?

00:02:58.644 --> 00:03:00.479
And Jane said,
"Well, let's foster them."

00:03:00.479 --> 00:03:02.214
And I went, "What are you --"

00:03:02.214 --> 00:03:04.550
"Well, it's better than
them being in a cage."

00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:06.151
And I knew it wouldn't end well.

00:03:06.151 --> 00:03:09.355
So we got this beautiful cat,
being fostered,

00:03:09.355 --> 00:03:12.825
a rescue cat, you know,
to find it a home,

00:03:12.825 --> 00:03:14.627
and it was sort of shy.

00:03:14.627 --> 00:03:17.596
Within one day, it got on my lap
and looked at me,

00:03:17.596 --> 00:03:19.265
and I went, "We're keeping it."

00:03:19.265 --> 00:03:20.599
You know?

00:03:20.599 --> 00:03:24.670
I was never going to --
How can I give it away now?

00:03:24.670 --> 00:03:27.440
No.
-What did you name the cat?

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:30.175
-Pickle.
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:30.175 --> 00:03:32.377
Pickle is a great name.
-Should I go and get her?

00:03:32.377 --> 00:03:33.812
Should I try to find her?

00:03:33.812 --> 00:03:35.280
-Yeah,
I would love to see Pickle.

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:37.750
Yes!
-She might struggle.

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:40.286
This might be --
She might knock the lights over.

00:03:40.286 --> 00:03:41.387
Let's have a -- Hold on.

00:03:41.387 --> 00:03:43.089
-This is very exciting.

00:03:43.089 --> 00:03:45.158
-Wanna be on "Jimmy Fallon"?

00:03:45.158 --> 00:03:47.726
He is not a moon-faced,
talentless hack.

00:03:47.726 --> 00:03:50.696
He's a very good...

00:03:50.696 --> 00:03:54.033
-Moon-faced, talented --
Oh, wow!

00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:56.769
Pickle, hi.

00:03:56.769 --> 00:03:59.405
Pickle, did you -- Oh, no, stop.

00:03:59.405 --> 00:04:01.340
This is honestly the cutest.

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:03.242
Oh, did she say something?

00:04:03.242 --> 00:04:06.211
Oh, stop it. Now look at --

00:04:06.211 --> 00:04:09.047
Oh, Ricky, this is --
Oh, I'm taken, as well.

00:04:09.047 --> 00:04:12.417
Everyone loves Pickle now.
Come on.

00:04:12.417 --> 00:04:14.720
Thank you. Hi, Pickle.
Welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:16.589
Thank you for coming on.

00:04:16.589 --> 00:04:19.058
-I won't stress her.
I'll let her go. Go on.

00:04:19.058 --> 00:04:20.559
-Oh, my gosh.

00:04:20.559 --> 00:04:22.461
You know, I wanted --

00:04:22.461 --> 00:04:24.998
-I showed Jimmy Fallon
my pickle.

00:04:24.998 --> 00:04:28.400
That's...

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:31.104
-Get in line, buddy.

00:04:33.439 --> 00:04:38.778
Hey, you're doing something fun
during quarantine on Twitter

00:04:38.778 --> 00:04:42.582
and Instagram, where, in part,

00:04:42.582 --> 00:04:45.151
you answer questions
from people.

00:04:45.151 --> 00:04:47.553
-Yeah, I just do this
a couple of times a week.

00:04:47.553 --> 00:04:49.455
I do this sort of thing live.

00:04:49.455 --> 00:04:52.458
I'm just here,
just talking to the people,

00:04:52.458 --> 00:04:54.126
and they're sending
me questions.

00:04:54.126 --> 00:04:56.429
And, you know, it's great.

00:04:56.429 --> 00:05:00.700
It's really great, because I
think it's the closest you get,

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:02.602
you know, to connect,
'cause, you know,

00:05:02.602 --> 00:05:03.803
you're actually talking to them,

00:05:03.803 --> 00:05:07.873
and they tune in,
you know, every time.

00:05:07.873 --> 00:05:09.542
It's great.
-What do they say so you?

00:05:09.542 --> 00:05:10.676
-I sort of did it
'cause I thought,

00:05:10.676 --> 00:05:11.710
"I should do something."

00:05:11.710 --> 00:05:14.546
But, actually, I like it.

00:05:14.546 --> 00:05:15.982
I like doing it now.

00:05:15.982 --> 00:05:19.885
I really like the -- you know,
the feeling of this little club.

00:05:19.885 --> 00:05:21.053
So it's great.

00:05:21.053 --> 00:05:24.257
And they send me questions
that range from

00:05:24.257 --> 00:05:26.759
philosophical questions
about the universe

00:05:26.759 --> 00:05:29.695
and life and death and all that
to stupid ones,

00:05:29.695 --> 00:05:31.030
like, you know,

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:36.935
"What if you had to swap
your mouth with your anus?"

00:05:36.935 --> 00:05:39.605
-Wow. That's --

00:05:39.605 --> 00:05:40.973
I'm going to just cross
that question off,

00:05:40.973 --> 00:05:43.709
'cause I was going to ask --

00:05:43.709 --> 00:05:45.511
I think I said, "I wouldn't
go to restaurants."

00:05:45.511 --> 00:05:50.349
-That was the next question.
[ Both laugh ]

00:05:50.349 --> 00:05:52.552
-But it's nice, as well,
'cause there's lots of, like,

00:05:52.552 --> 00:05:56.355
cats and dogs on Twitter,
and I love it

00:05:56.355 --> 00:05:58.323
when they ask me a question
from their perspective.

00:05:58.323 --> 00:06:04.429
Like, one dog asked me,
"You've got a lot of awards,

00:06:04.429 --> 00:06:06.832
but have you ever found
a really good stick?"

00:06:06.832 --> 00:06:08.467
And stuff like that.

00:06:08.467 --> 00:06:11.204
-Yeah, let's get down to
the brass tacks.

00:06:11.204 --> 00:06:12.438
Have you ever had
a really good stick, man?

00:06:12.438 --> 00:06:13.739
Come on. That's awesome.

00:06:13.739 --> 00:06:16.008
-Have you ever stuck your head
out of a car window

00:06:16.008 --> 00:06:18.777
when it's going really fast?

00:06:18.777 --> 00:06:21.013
-That's living it up, man.

00:06:21.013 --> 00:06:24.716
Ricky, I want to talk about your
television series, "After Life."

00:06:24.716 --> 00:06:25.918
Man, I love this show.

00:06:25.918 --> 00:06:28.020
Second season.
You're great in it.

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:30.489
I was saying earlier, you know,
it's a very funny show,

00:06:30.489 --> 00:06:36.695
but it's also heartbreaking and
dealing with loss and grief.

00:06:36.695 --> 00:06:38.297
And I love the balance
that you do there,

00:06:38.297 --> 00:06:41.033
but I think only you can do it.

00:06:41.033 --> 00:06:43.569
The two seasons are
on Netflix now,

00:06:43.569 --> 00:06:47.039
so if anyone hasn't seen it,
they should check it out.

00:06:47.039 --> 00:06:48.440
But, I mean,
you're getting a little --

00:06:48.440 --> 00:06:51.043
a kind of pre-awards buzz

00:06:51.043 --> 00:06:53.512
for Season 2,
so congrats on that.

00:06:53.512 --> 00:06:55.882
I heard there's going to be
a Season 3 on the show.

00:06:55.882 --> 00:06:58.717
What can you tell us?
Are you writing it?

00:06:58.717 --> 00:07:00.620
-I've sort of written it,
you know?

00:07:00.620 --> 00:07:02.989
I had more time this year
than I thought I'd have.

00:07:02.989 --> 00:07:06.859
So, I wasn't sure about it.

00:07:06.859 --> 00:07:09.694
You know, I knew Netflix wanted
a third season,

00:07:09.694 --> 00:07:10.963
but, you know, they would

00:07:10.963 --> 00:07:13.733
because, you know, the first two
were successful,

00:07:13.733 --> 00:07:16.802
but I wanted to make sure it
wasn't an unwanted encore.

00:07:16.802 --> 00:07:18.470
So I said, "We'll see."

00:07:18.470 --> 00:07:20.906
And after about a week
when the Season 2 came out,

00:07:20.906 --> 00:07:23.943
they called and said,
"Listen, let's do a third."

00:07:23.943 --> 00:07:28.314
-I was going to show a clip of
"After Life" from Season 2,

00:07:28.314 --> 00:07:29.414
but this is fun.

00:07:29.414 --> 00:07:30.983
Right before we started
the show,

00:07:30.983 --> 00:07:32.818
you said,
"Let me just send you this."

00:07:32.818 --> 00:07:35.688
It's an outtake from Season 2.

00:07:35.688 --> 00:07:37.156
And I love that you sent this.

00:07:37.156 --> 00:07:38.390
Tell us what
we're going to see here.

00:07:38.390 --> 00:07:40.392
It's very, very funny.

00:07:40.392 --> 00:07:44.863
-Well, as you know, my leading
lady is a German shepherd.

00:07:44.863 --> 00:07:48.300
And it's just fun all the time.

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:51.136
We do the take,
and then things happen.

00:07:51.136 --> 00:07:53.939
And I don't know why
she did this,

00:07:53.939 --> 00:07:55.640
but it was after a take.

00:07:55.640 --> 00:07:59.512
This dog suddenly decided
to show how much she loved me.

00:07:59.512 --> 00:08:00.646
-Let's take a look at this.

00:08:00.646 --> 00:08:02.615
Here's Ricky Gervais
and his co-star.

00:08:08.621 --> 00:08:09.889
-Good girl.

00:08:12.091 --> 00:08:14.360
Alright, that's enough. Right.

00:08:14.360 --> 00:08:15.928
Okay. Okay.

00:08:15.928 --> 00:08:17.396
Yeah, I'm going to
have a shower.

00:08:17.396 --> 00:08:19.332
Cheers. Down.

00:08:19.332 --> 00:08:23.201
Bad girl, Brandy. Bad girl.
Bad girl, Brandy.

00:08:23.201 --> 00:08:25.238
[ Laughs ]

00:08:34.947 --> 00:08:36.549
-Almost.

00:08:40.987 --> 00:08:44.089
-Thank you.

00:08:44.089 --> 00:08:47.059
It's like,
for the first couple of seconds,

00:08:47.059 --> 00:08:48.928
I tried to stay in character.

00:08:48.928 --> 00:08:54.066
I sort of laughed and said,
Brandy, like, her stage name,

00:08:54.066 --> 00:08:55.434
and then I thought,

00:08:55.434 --> 00:08:57.002
"We can't use this."

00:08:57.002 --> 00:08:59.371
It looks mental."
Oh!

00:08:59.371 --> 00:09:03.609
But I should say, to be fair,

00:09:03.609 --> 00:09:07.212
all the actors do that to me
after a take.

00:09:07.212 --> 00:09:09.482
They love me so much.

00:09:09.482 --> 00:09:10.683
-Ah! See?

00:09:10.683 --> 00:09:13.052
That right there deserves
an award right there.

00:09:13.052 --> 00:09:14.953
That scene right there
is what I love.

00:09:14.953 --> 00:09:16.455
I love that she finished.

00:09:16.455 --> 00:09:18.624
She goes -- Finally like a
couple more licks.

00:09:18.624 --> 00:09:19.792
"Alright, I'm done."

00:09:19.792 --> 00:09:22.661
And perfect timing --
you go, "Thank you."

00:09:22.661 --> 00:09:23.929
It's so good.

00:09:23.929 --> 00:09:26.064
Ricky Gervais, the first
two seasons of "After Life"

00:09:26.064 --> 00:09:27.366
are on Netflix now.

